From 8b62921a908a541098949eca813243e7bdd28577 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:10:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 33/41] Import and export library packages (parts-site zips)

File > Import Library Package... takes the zip a parts site (SnapEDA, Ultra Librarian,
SamacSys, Digi-Key, Mouser...) offers for KiCad and makes the part usable in one step: the
symbol libraries, footprints and 3D models are unpacked into the 3rd-party folder (all
projects) or into the project (this project), the footprints' 3D model paths (usually a path on
the author's disk) are pointed at the unpacked models, the symbols' Footprint fields at the
footprint libraries as registered, and the libraries are added to the library tables and
reloaded in the open editors.  Importing the same zip again updates it.  Zip entries that would
land outside the package are refused (PROJECT_ARCHIVER::Unarchive).

File > Export Library Package... writes the reverse: a symbol library (a .kicad_sym, or a
.kicad_symdir merged), the footprints its symbols name and their 3D models, with the model
paths pointing into the zip, so a part moves between devices or to someone else.

Both are also MCP tools (kicad_import_library_package, kicad_export_library_package).  On
Android there is no other practical way to bring in a downloaded part: Configure Paths cannot
be edited and the library table grids are hard to use with a finger.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
